### One Important Caveat: Web Target

On the **web target**, `flutter_webrtc` wraps the browser's native WebRTC APIs via `dart:js` [[19]](https://github.com/flutter-webrtc/dart-webrtc). This means:
- ✅ DataChannels work identically
- ✅ MediaTracks work identically
- ✅ ICE/STUN/TURN work identically
- ❌ **No raw UDP sockets** (same constraint as pure browser JS)

So the same browser limitations we discussed earlier apply — ephemeral WebRTC connections for probing new peers, DataChannel ping-pong for existing ones. But the **architecture is identical** whether you're on mobile, desktop, or web.

