### Why This Is Better

| Aspect | Compression-as-Decay | Timing Wheel |
|--------|---------------------|--------------|
| **Predictability** | Emergent, depends on bucket fill | Explicit TTL, configurable |
| **Granularity** | Coarse (halving events) | Fine (per-slot, e.g., 60s) |
| **Refresh** | Impossible — entries are anonymous | Natural — just move to new slot |
| **Complexity** | Tied to EBF internals | Clean separation of concerns |
| **Debugging** | "Why did that entry disappear?" | "Its TTL expired at time T" |

The timing wheel is also a known, battle-tested pattern (Linux kernel timers, Kafka, Netty) — no novel research needed.

