## Corrected Shedding Logic

```
EXHALE (80%+):
  Scan all entries, sort by ejection_date ASC (oldest first)
  Push blocks out until capacity reaches 50%

  A block at fib=10 with ejection_date 3 weeks ago → SHED
  A block at fib=0 with ejection_date 5 minutes ago  → KEPT
```

This is the right separation of concerns:

| Signal | Scope | Drives |
|--------|-------|--------|
| **Fibonacci rank** | Global (gossiped) | What to *seek*, what to use in new representations, what to replicate |
| **Ejection date** | Local (per-node) | What to *shed* when space is tight |

A block can be globally beloved (fib=12) but if this particular node hasn't touched it in weeks, it's dead weight locally. Meanwhile a fib=0 block that was just created and is actively being used stays.

