### Ejection Date Lifecycle

```c
// On block creation
entry->ejection_date = now() + DEFAULT_TTL;  // e.g., 7 days from now

// On block access (index_get → _index_increment)
// Extend the lease — this block is locally useful
index_entry_set_ejection_date(entry, now() + DEFAULT_TTL);

// On exhalation
void exhale_blocks(index_t* index, block_cache_t* cache) {
  // Collect all entries
  index_entry_vec_t* all = index_to_array(index);

  // Sort by ejection_date ascending (oldest first)
  qsort(all->data, all->length, sizeof(index_entry_t*), compare_ejection_date);

  size_t to_free = blocks_to_reach_target(index, 0.50);
  for (size_t i = 0; i < all->length && to_free > 0; i++) {
    index_entry_t* entry = all->data[i];
    push_block_to_network(cache, entry);
    index_remove(index, entry->hash);
    to_free--;
  }
}
```

The fib rank still matters — when the receiving node evaluates the incoming Push, it checks the block's fib against its own local ranks to decide whether to accept. A high-fib block being shed from one node is a gift to another.

