## Integrated Find_Value Algorithm

### Message Structure

```c
typedef struct {
  rpc_header_t  header;
  buffer_t*     block_hash;         // what we're looking for
  uint8_t       ttl;                // remaining hops
  buffer_t*     visited_bloom;      // negative information (Quasar)
  size_t        visited_count;

  // SoPPSoN path recording for feedback
  node_id_t     path[MAX_PATH];     // nodes this request has traversed
  uint8_t       path_len;           // how many nodes in the path
  uint64_t      start_time;         // when the search began (for learning rate γ)
} find_value_msg_t;
```

### The Algorithm

```plaintext
HANDLE-FIND-VALUE(msg, socket):
  block_hash = msg.block_hash

  // ── STEP 1: Check local ──
  entry = index_peek(self.index, block_hash)
  if entry != NULL:
    // SUCCESS — respond and apply all learning rules
    SEND-FIND-VALUE-RESPONSE({
      found:   true,
      holder:  self.id,
      fib:     entry.counter.fib,
      path:    msg.path,        // return the path for feedback
      latency: now() - msg.start_time
    })
    index_increment(self.index, entry)
    return

  // ── STEP 2: TTL check ──
  if msg.ttl == 0:
    REMEMBER-FAILED-REQUEST(self.memories[msg.source], block_hash)
    SEND-FIND-VALUE-RESPONSE({ found: false, path: msg.path })
    return

  // ── STEP 3: Record self in path and visited set ──
  msg.path[msg.path_len++] = self.id
  bloom_insert(msg.visited_bloom, self.id)
  msg.visited_count++
  msg.ttl--

  // ── STEP 4: Gather candidates from rings ──
  candidates = gather_candidates({
    rings:       [ring_for_distance - 1, ring_for_distance, ring_for_distance + 1],
    min_weight:  0.01,              // low bar — roulette handles filtering
    exclude:     msg.visited_bloom  // negative information
  })

  if candidates is empty:
    REMEMBER-FAILED-REQUEST(self.memories[msg.source], block_hash)
    SEND-FIND-VALUE-RESPONSE({ found: false, path: msg.path })
    return

  // ── STEP 5: Roulette-wheel selection (SoPPSoN) ──
  // Build cumulative probability distribution
  total_weight = sum(c. weight for c in candidates)
  for i = 0; i < FORWARD_FANOUT; i++:
    r = random() * total_weight
    selected = find_in_cumulative(candidates, r)
    if selected != null:
      forward msg to selected
      // Remove from candidates to avoid duplicate forwards
      candidates.remove(selected)
      total_weight -= selected.weight
```

### Roulette-Wheel Selection

```c
node_id_t roulette_select(peer_vec_t* candidates, float total_weight) {
  float r = random_float() * total_weight;
  float cumulative = 0.0;

  for (size_t i = 0; i < candidates->length; i++) {
    cumulative += candidates->data[i].weight;
    if (r <= cumulative) {
      return candidates->data[i].id;
    }
  }
  // Fallback (floating point edge case)
  return candidates->data[candidates->length - 1].id;
}
```

This means a peer with weight 0.8 gets ~80% of selections, but a peer with weight 0.05 still gets ~5%. The network explores.

