## Why Roulette-Wheel Matters

Consider two peers B and C in A's ring:

| Peer | Weight | Roulette probability | Always-pick-best |
|------|--------|---------------------|------------------|
| B | 0.80 | 80% | 100% |
| C | 0.20 | 20% | 0% |

With "always pick best," C never gets traffic, never proves itself, and its weight never grows. The system converges prematurely on B.

With roulette-wheel, C gets ~20% of queries. If C routes well, its weight grows. If C routes poorly, its weight decays. The system **explores and exploits simultaneously**.

This is exactly what SoPPSoN demonstrated: the combination of Frequency + Feedback + Symmetry rules, with roulette-wheel selection, converges to the correct social graph even when starting from random connections.

