## Composite Score Computation

```c
float compute_storage_score(node_t* self, ring_member_t* peer, store_msg_t* msg) {
  // Factor 1: Hebbian weight — proven useful peer
  float w = peer->weight;

  // Factor 2: Available capacity — more room = better
  float capacity_factor = 1.0 - peer->capacity;
  if (peer->capacity >= 0.80) {
    capacity_factor *= 0.1;  // heavily penalize nodes in exhale phase
  }

  // Factor 3: Latency proximity — closer = faster future retrievals
  float latency_factor = 1.0 / (1.0 + peer->latency / LATENCY_NORMALIZATION_MS);

  // Factor 4: Availability — reliable nodes are better homes
  float availability = get_peer_availability(peer->id);

  // Factor 5: Portfolio fit — does this peer already hold related blocks?
  // (Optional: if we track block relationships, prefer nodes with
  //  blocks that are often retrieved together with this one)
  float portfolio_fit = 1.0;  // neutral if not tracked

  // Combined score
  float score = w * capacity_factor * latency_factor * availability * portfolio_fit;

  return score;
}
```

