## Response Handling with Hebbian Updates

```plaintext
HANDLE-STORE-RESPONSE(msg, socket):
  if msg.accepted:
    // ── SUCCESS: Apply learning rules ──

    τ = msg.latency
    γ = γ₀ · max(0, 1 - τ / T) · q_store
    Δw = γ

    requester = msg.path[0]
    storer = msg.holder

    // FREQUENCY RULE: requester → storer
    if self.id == requester:
      w_{self → storer} += Δw

    // FEEDBACK RULE: intermediate forwarders
    for i = 1; i < msg.path_len - 1; i++:
      if self.id == msg.path[i]:
        w_{self → msg.path[i + 1]} += η_f · Δw

    // SYMMETRY RULE: reverse direction
    for i = 0; i < msg.path_len - 1; i++:
      if self.id == msg.path[i]:
        w_{msg.path[i + 1] → self} += η_s · Δw

    // Track that this peer stored for us (availability signal)
    record_storage_event(msg.holder, msg.block_hash)

  else:
    // ── PARTIAL OR FULL FAILURE ──
    // If replicas still needed, the original requester can retry
    // with adjusted parameters (wider ring search, lower bar)
    if msg.replicas_remaining > 0:
      schedule_retry(msg.block_hash, msg.replicas_remaining)
```

