## How Metrics Flow

```
                    ┌─────────────────────────────┐
                    │      PASSIVE (Gossip)        │
                    │                              │
                    │  Each gossip cycle carries:  │
                    │  - source.capacity           │
                    │  - samples[].capacity        │
                    │                              │
                    │  Stored in ring_member_t     │
                    │  Updated every ~30-60s       │
                    └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                                   │
                    ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
                    │      ACTIVE (Ping)           │
                    │                              │
                    │  PING / PING_RESPONSE:       │
                    │  - latency measurement       │
                    │  - liveness check            │
                    │  - updates availability EWMA │
                    │                              │
                    │  CAPACITY_QUERY (new):       │
                    │  - explicit capacity poll    │
                    │  - used when gossip data     │
                    │    is stale or critical      │
                    └──────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## When to Use Which

| Situation | Data Source | Rationale |
|-----------|------------|-----------|
| Routine Store forwarding | Gossip capacity (cached in ring member) | Good enough; ±30s staleness is fine |
| Last replica, must succeed | Direct `CAPACITY_QUERY` before forwarding | Don't waste hops on a full node |
| Peer hasn't gossiped in >2 min | Direct `CAPACITY_QUERY` | Data is stale, verify before trusting |
| Peer has `consecutive_fails ≥ 2` | Skip entirely | Probably offline, don't bother |
| Exhalation Push | Gossip capacity is sufficient | If rejected, try next candidate |

