## Availability EWMA from Ping

The existing `PING` / `PING_RESPONSE` already gives you latency and liveness. The availability score builds passively from every ping exchange:

```c
void on_ping_response(node_t* self, node_id_t peer, uint32_t latency_ms) {
  ring_member_t* m = find_ring_member(self, peer);
  if (m == NULL) return;

  m->latency = latency_ms;  // update Meridian ring placement

  peer_availability_t* av = get_availability(self, peer);
  av->last_seen = now();
  av->consecutive_fails = 0;

  // EWMA update (decay old data, weight new observation)
  float alpha = 0.1;
  av->availability = alpha * 1.0 + (1 - alpha) * av->availability;
}

void on_ping_timeout(node_t* self, node_id_t peer) {
  peer_availability_t* av = get_availability(self, peer);
  av->consecutive_fails++;

  float alpha = 0.1;
  av->availability = alpha * 0.0 + (1 - alpha) * av->availability;
}
```

No new message type needed — the existing ping infrastructure accumulates availability as a side effect.

