## Per-Connection Rate Limit Table

Each node maintains one set of buckets per connected peer:

```c
typedef struct {
  node_id_t       peer_id;
  float           weight;          // current Hebbian w_{self→peer}

  token_bucket_t  find_value;      // cheap: lookups
  token_bucket_t  store;           // expensive: writes
  token_bucket_t  push;            // expensive: incoming blocks
  token_bucket_t  seek;            // moderate: listing blocks
  token_bucket_t  pull;            // expensive: outgoing blocks
  token_bucket_t  gossip;          // cheap: always allow

  uint64_t        last_advertised; // when we last sent limits to peer
} peer_rate_limits_t;
```

