## Default Rate Configuration

```c
typedef struct {
  float     base_rate;       // per second
  float     max_rate;        // per second at weight=1.0
  float     burst_size;      // max accumulated tokens
  float     cost;            // tokens consumed per operation
} rate_limit_config_t;

// Node-wide defaults
const rate_limit_config_t RATE_CONFIGS[] = {
  [RPC_FIND_VALUE]   = { 5.0,  50.0,  20.0,  1.0  },  // cheap
  [RPC_STORE]        = { 0.5,  5.0,   3.0,   1.0  },  // expensive
  [RPC_PUSH]         = { 0.5,  5.0,   3.0,   1.0  },  // expensive
  [RPC_SEEK]         = { 1.0,  10.0,  5.0,   1.0  },  // moderate
  [RPC_PULL]         = { 1.0,  10.0,  5.0,   1.0  },  // moderate
  [RPC_GOSSIP]       = { 10.0, 10.0,  10.0,  0.1  },  // always allow
  [RPC_PING]         = { 10.0, 10.0,  10.0,  0.1  },  // always allow
};
```

A new peer with weight 0.0 gets the base rate. A long-trusted peer with weight 0.9 gets near the max rate. The burst size allows short spikes (e.g., a batch of related lookups) without penalty.

