## Advertising Limits to Peers

Limits are piggybacked on existing responses so senders learn their budget without extra messages:

```c
typedef struct {
  rpc_type_e   type;
  float        tokens_per_second;   // current refill rate
  float        burst_remaining;     // how much burst is left
  uint32_t     rejected_recently;   // count of recent rejections
} rate_limit_info_t;

// Appended to PING_RESPONSE, GOSSIP_RESPONSE, and any RATE_LIMITED message
```

On receiving this, the sender updates its local view:

```c
void update_remote_limits(node_t* self, node_id_t peer, rate_limit_info_t* info) {
  remote_rate_limits_t* remote = get_remote_limits(self, peer);
  remote->buckets[info->type].rate = info->tokens_per_second;
  remote->buckets[info->type].burst = info->burst_remaining;

  // If peer is rejecting, self-throttle preemptively
  if (info->rejected_recently > 0) {
    remote->backoff_until[info->type] = now() + BACKOFF_BASE_MS * info->rejected_recently;
  }
}
```

---

## Sender-Side Self-Throttling

Before sending, the originator checks its local copy of the remote peer's limits:

```c
bool can_send_to(node_t* self, node_id_t peer, rpc_type_e type) {
  remote_rate_limits_t* remote = get_remote_limits(self, peer);

  // Are we in backoff?
  if (now() < remote->backoff_until[type]) {
    return false;
  }

  // Do we estimate the peer has tokens?
  if (remote->buckets[type].burst < RATE_CONFIGS[type].cost) {
    return false;  // probably rate limited, skip this peer
  }

  return true;
}
```

This means the roulette-wheel selection in both Find_Value and Store naturally skips peers that are near their limits. The sender doesn't even try.

---

## Integration with Store Candidate Selection

```c
void forward_store(store_msg_t* msg) {
  candidates = gather_candidates_from_rings(msg);

  viable = [];
  for each c in candidates:
    // Skip if we know this peer is rate-limiting us
    if not can_send_to(self, c.id, RPC_STORE):
      continue;

    // Skip if peer is in exhale phase
    if c.phase == EXHALE:
      continue;

    // Skip if peer has been unreachable
    if c.consecutive_fails >= MAX_FAILS:
      continue;

    viable.push(c);

  // Roulette-wheel from viable only
  forward_via_roulette(msg, viable);
}
```

