## 9. Scalability

### 9.1 Homogeneous Protocol

The same protocol operates at every scale:

```c
/*
 * All deployment tiers use the same:
 *   - Transaction format (transaction_t)
 *   - Wire format (TLV encoding)
 *   - Cryptographic primitives (Ed25519, SHA-256, ABE, STARKs)
 *   - Protocol state machines (invoice, contract, legacy)
 *   - Attribute Machine (same CRDT merge)
 *
 * Only the deployment topology differs:
 *   - Wallet: single process, SQLite
 *   - Node: single process, PostgreSQL
 *   - Enterprise: sharded cluster, Raft, coordinator
 */
```

### 9.2 Deployment Tiers

```c
/* Tier 1: Spark Wallet (individual) */
typedef struct {
    party_t         party;
    smt_t           smt;            /* SQLite-backed */
    tx_log_t        tx_log;
    attribute_machine_t am;
    sequencer_t     sequencer;      /* Trivial: sequential */
    sqlite3        *db;
} spark_wallet_t;

/* Tier 2: Spark Node (small business) */
typedef struct {
    party_t         party;
    smt_t           smt;            /* PostgreSQL-backed */
    tx_log_t        tx_log;
    attribute_machine_t am;
    sequencer_t     sequencer;      /* Per-account nonces */
    PGconn         *db;
    uint32_t        account_count;
} spark_node_t;

/* Tier 3: Spark Enterprise (large organization) */
typedef struct {
    uint32_t        shard_count;
    shard_t        *shards;         /* Each: SMT + log + Raft */
    coordinator_t   coordinator;    /* Routes + cross-shard 2PC */
    attribute_machine_t am;         /* CRDT-replicated */
} spark_enterprise_t;

typedef struct {
    uint32_t        shard_id;
    smt_t           smt;
    tx_log_t        tx_log;
    raft_state_t    raft;           /* 3-node Raft cluster */
} shard_t;
```

### 9.3 Cross-Shard Transactions

Enterprise deployments handle cross-shard transactions via two-phase commit:

```c
/*
 * Algorithm: CROSS_SHARD_TRANSACTION
 *
 * 1. Coordinator receives transaction
 * 2. Coordinator determines affected shards
 * 3. Coordinator sends PREPARE to each shard
 * 4. Each shard validates and reserves (locks accounts)
 * 5. If all shards respond PREPARED:
 *    a. Coordinator sends COMMIT to all shards
 *    b. Each shard applies the transaction
 * 6. If any shard responds ABORT:
 *    a. Coordinator sends ROLLBACK to all shards
 *    b. Each shard releases locks
 * 7. Coordinator logs the outcome
 */

int enterprise_cross_shard_tx(spark_enterprise_t *ent,
                              const transaction_t *tx) {
    uint32_t shards_affected[MAX_SHARDS];
    uint32_t shard_count = identify_affected_shards(ent, tx,
                                                     shards_affected);

    /* Phase 1: Prepare */
    int all_prepared = 1;
    for (int i = 0; i < shard_count; i++) {
        prepare_result_t result;
        shard_prepare(&ent->shards[shards_affected[i]], tx, &result);
        if (result != PREPARE_OK) {
            all_prepared = 0;
            break;
        }
    }

    /* Phase 2: Commit or Rollback */
    if (all_prepared) {
        for (int i = 0; i < shard_count; i++)
            shard_commit(&ent->shards[shards_affected[i]], tx);
    } else {
        for (int i = 0; i < shard_count; i++)
            shard_rollback(&ent->shards[shards_affected[i]], tx);
    }

    return all_prepared ? 0 : -1;
}
```

### 9.4 The External Interface

Regardless of deployment tier, the external interface is the same:

```c
/*
 * Any party, regardless of scale, sends and receives
 * the same message format. The recipient does not know
 * (or need to know) whether the sender is a wallet or
 * an enterprise cluster.
 */

int send_transaction(const transaction_t *tx,
                     const uint8_t recipient_id[32]) {
    uint8_t buffer[MAX_MSG_SIZE];
    uint32_t buf_len;

    message_serialize(tx, MSG_TRANSACTION,
                     local_party_id, recipient_id,
                     sig_vtable, signing_key, signing_key_len,
                     buffer, &buf_len);

    return network_send(recipient_id, buffer, buf_len);
}
```

