The system has TWO classes of attributes:
1. IMMUTABLE attributes — issued by the central authority (e.g., "id:0x7F3A", "role:verified")
2. USER-MANAGED attributes — self-asserted by the user (e.g., "name:John", "address:123_Main_St")

Users receive a base key from the authority with immutable attributes, then EXTEND it 
using OABE_delegate() to add their own attributes. The delegation mechanism cryptographically 
binds user-managed attributes to the user's identity — they cannot be transferred to another user.

Policies can reference BOTH attribute types:
  "(id:0x7F3A) AND (name:John OR name:J_Smith)"

## OPENABE-C API REFERENCE

This is the complete API surface you have to work with:

=== Initialization ===
  OABE_initialize() / OABE_shutdown()

