### README.md

```markdown
# Hybrid ABE — Authority + User-Managed Attributes

A C implementation of CP-ABE with **dual-attribute-source** support, built on openabe-c.

## Architecture

This system extends standard CP-ABE with two classes of attributes:

| Attribute Type | Issued By | Mutable By | Example |
|:---|---:|:---:|:---|
| **Immutable** | Central Authority | No one | `id:0x7F3A`, `role:verified` |
| **User-Managed** | User (self-asserted) | User only | `name:John`, `address:123_Main_St` |

Users receive a **base key** from the authority containing only immutable attributes.
They then **extend** it via cryptographic delegation to add their own attributes.

Policies can reference both types:
```
(id:alice) AND (name:Alice_Smith OR name:A_Smith)
```

## Building

```bash
# Prerequisites: openabe, pbc, gmp, cmake, pkg-config

mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
cmake --build .
```

## Testing

```bash
# Run all tests
ctest

# Run with verbose output
ctest --output-on-failure -V

# Run a specific test
ctest -R test_user_extend_decrypt -V

# Build and test
cmake --build . && ctest --output-on-failure
```

## API Overview

| Function | Description |
|:---|---|
| `hybrid_abe_global_init()` | Initialize the library (call once) |
| `hybrid_abe_setup()` | Generate master public/secret keys |
| `hybrid_abe_authority_issue_key()` | Issue base key with immutable attrs |
| `hybrid_abe_user_extend_key()` | Extend key with user-managed attrs |
| `hybrid_abe_user_update_attributes()` | Re-delegate with new user attrs |
| `hybrid_abe_encrypt()` | Encrypt under a policy |
| `hybrid_abe_decrypt()` | Decrypt with a key |

## Security Model

- **Collusion resistance**: Keys are randomized per-user. Two users cannot combine keys.
- **Immutable attributes**: Cannot be removed or modified by the user (cryptographically enforced).
- **User attributes**: Self-asserted. Policy authors should combine them with immutable attrs for trust.
- **No revocation**: This scheme does not implement attribute revocation. Use key rotation for that.

## Dependencies

- [openabe-c](https://github.com/nick-bauer/openabe-c) — C wrapper for OpenABE
- PBC (Pairing-Based Cryptography) library
- GMP (GNU Multiple Precision Arithmetic Library)
- CMake ≥ 3.16
```

