## The Static Assumption I Made

In my earlier sketch, the vault was populated **all at once**:

```c
// Static approach — populate once, know everyone upfront
crable_vault_populate(state, mpk, mpk_len, users, user_count);
//                                          ↑ all users known at once
```

This implies you need the complete user list at setup time. **But that's not necessary.**

---

## The Dynamic Approach: Add Users Anytime 🕐

The vault is just a **mapping**: `(operation, user_id) → encrypted_signing_key`. You can add entries one at a time, at any point.

### Revised API

```c
/* Add a SINGLE user to the vault after state machine is running.
   Can be called at any time — before or after transitions. */
int crable_vault_add_user(
    crable_state_t *state,
    const uint8_t *mpk, size_t mpk_len,
    const char *user_id,
    const uint8_t *user_sk_ecdsa, size_t sk_len,
    const char *attr_string
);

/* Remove a user from the vault (revocation).
   After this, they can no longer sign transitions. */
int crable_vault_remove_user(
    crable_state_t *state,
    const char *user_id
);
```

### How the Vault Actually Works

```plaintext
The vault is just a dynamic data structure:

Vault = {
    ("write", "alice") → ABE_encrypt(sk_alice, "user_id:alice"),
    ("write", "bob")   → ABE_encrypt(sk_bob,   "user_id:bob"),
    ("write", "carol") → ABE_encrypt(sk_carol, "user_id:carol"),
    ("read",  "alice") → ABE_encrypt(sk_alice, "user_id:alice"),
    ("read",  "bob")   → ABE_encrypt(sk_bob,   "user_id:bob"),
    ...
}

Adding a user = insert new rows into this mapping
Removing a user = delete their rows
```

### Adding a User After the State Machine is Running

```c
// Day 1: Create state machine with initial users
crable_setup(&state, &mpk, &mpk_len, &msk, &msk_len);

// Register Alice
crable_register_user(msk, msk_len, mpk, mpk_len,
                     "alice", "role:author", ...);

// Add Alice to vault
crable_vault_add_user(state, mpk, mpk_len,
                      "alice", alice_sk_ecdsa, sizeof(alice_sk_ecdsa),
                      "role:author");

// Alice starts working — transitions happen...

// Day 2: Bob joins the team (state machine already has 50 transitions)
crable_register_user(msk, msk_len, mpk, mpk_len,
                     "bob", "role:reviewer", ...);

crable_vault_add_user(state, mpk, mpk_len,
                      "bob", bob_sk_ecdsa, sizeof(bob_sk_ecdsa),
                      "role:reviewer");

// Bob can now sign transitions immediately — no re-setup needed
```

