## Summary: Static vs Dynamic 📊

| Aspect | Static (my earlier sketch) | Dynamic (what you want) |
|:---|---:|:---:|
| **User registration** | All at setup | **Anytime** |
| **Vault population** | One bulk call | **Add/remove individual users** |
| **Policy changes** | Fixed at genesis | **Via transitions (logged)** |
| **Verification** | Checks fixed user list | **Checks current user list** |
| **Revocation** | Not supported | **Remove from vault + user list** |
| **Future-proofing** | Must predict all users | **Handles unknown future users** |

The protocol is **inherently dynamic** — I just presented the static version for simplicity. The dynamic version is actually **easier to implement** because you don't need to batch everything at setup.

