## The Locking Primitive 🔒

Since resources have scarcity, locking is a **primitive** that operations **compose**:

### Lock Acquisition

```c
// Step 1: Acquire lock (primitive operation)
crabs_operation_t lock_op = {
    .type = "__lock__",           // Built-in primitive
    .payload = "treasury",
    .writes = {"__locks__"},      // Internal lock registry
    .policy = "role:admin OR role:member",  // Who can lock
    .lamport_time = 2000,
    .signature = {...}
};

// State machine handles this internally:
//   - Generates random lock_token
//   - Records lock in __locks__ CRDT
//   - Sets expiration
//   - Returns lock_token to caller
```

### Composing Lock + Operation

```c
// User does this in sequence:

// 1. Lock
lock_result = crabs_send_and_wait(state, lock_op);
// → receives lock_token = 0xA3F7...

// 2. Perform operation WITH lock token
crabs_operation_t transfer_op = {
    .type = "transfer",
    .payload = "{ \"amount\": 10, \"to\": \"bob\" }",
    .reads = {"treasury"},
    .writes = {"treasury"},
    .lock_claims = {
        {.resource = "treasury", .lock_token = 0xA3F7...}
    },
    .policy = "role:admin",
    .signature = {...}
};

// 3. Unlock (primitive)
crabs_operation_t unlock_op = {
    .type = "__unlock__",
    .payload = "treasury",
    .lock_token = 0xA3F7...,
    .writes = {"__locks__"},
    .policy = "role:admin OR role:member",
    .signature = {...}
};
```

### Lock Verification in the State Machine

```c
int crabs_verify_lock(state, resource, token) {
    lock_entry = crabs_read(state, "__locks__", resource);

    if (!lock_entry.exists)
        return CRABS_ERR_NOT_LOCKED;
    if (lock_entry.token != token)
        return CRABS_ERR_WRONG_TOKEN;
    if (lock_entry.expired)
        return CRABS_ERR_LOCK_EXPIRED;
    if (lock_entry.owner != op.signer_id && op.signer_id != "")
        return CRABS_ERR_WRONG_OWNER;

    return CRABS_SUCCESS;
}
```

