## The Verification Step: Where Invariants Are Checked

The `__verify__` primitive is where **type invariants** are enforced:

```c
int crabs_verify_resource(crabs_state_t *state, const char *resource) {
    crabs_resource_t *res = crabs_get_resource(state, resource);

    // Check ALL invariants defined for this resource's type
    for (int i = 0; i < res->type->invariant_count; i++) {
        crabs_invariant_t *inv = &res->type->invariants[i];

        switch (inv->type) {
            case CRABS_INV_GREATER_THAN:
                if (res->value <= inv->int_value) {
                    return CRABS_ERR_INVARIANT_VIOLATED;
                }
                break;
            case CRABS_INV_DIVISIBLE_BY:
                if (res->value % inv->int_value != 0) {
                    return CRABS_ERR_INVARIANT_VIOLATED;
                }
                break;
            // ... other invariants
        }
    }

    return CRABS_SUCCESS;
}
```

If `__verify__` fails, the resource goes to an error state, and the only valid next operation is `__rollback__`:

```c
// Verification failed → rollback
crabs_operation_t rollback = {
    .type = "__rollback__",
    .resources = {"treasury"},
    .required_state = {"treasury": "modified"},  // or "verified"?
    .next_state = {"treasury": "idle"},
    // Rollback restores the pre-lock snapshot
};
```

