## The Lock Extension Mechanism

Sometimes an operation genuinely needs more time. The lock holder can **extend** the lock — but only up to a limit:

```c
/*
 * __extend_lock__ primitive
 *
 * Only the lock holder can extend.
 * Limited to max_lock_extensions times.
 */

int crabs_primitive_extend_lock(crabs_state_t *state,
                                 const char *resource,
                                 const uint8_t *lock_token,
                                 const char *requester_id) {

    crabs_resource_t *res = crabs_get_resource(state, resource);

    // Step 1: Verify caller holds the lock
    if (memcmp(res->lock_token, lock_token, 32) != 0) {
        return CRABS_ERR_LOCK_TOKEN_MISMATCH;
    }

    if (strcmp(res->lock_owner, requester_id) != 0) {
        return CRABS_ERR_LOCK_OWNER_MISMATCH;
    }

    // Step 2: Check extension limit
    if (res->lock_extensions >= state->config.lock.max_lock_extensions) {
        return CRABS_ERR_MAX_EXTENSIONS_REACHED;
    }

    // Step 3: Extend
    res->lock_expiry = crabs_now() + state->config.lock.max_lock_duration_ms;
    res->lock_extensions++;

    return CRABS_SUCCESS;
}
```

