## The Transform Matrix for Ordered Sets

This is the foundation. Every other type builds on it.

```plaintext
              | INSERT(i)  | DELETE(i)  | MOVE(i→j)  | SWAP(i,j)
──────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────
INSERT(k)     | priority   | shift_left | shift_left | shift_left
              | compare    | if k > i   | if k > i   | if k > min(i,j)
──────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────
DELETE(k)     | shift_right| no_conflict| adjust     | adjust
              | if k >= i  | (same pos) |            |
──────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────
MOVE(k→l)     | shift_right| shift_left | composite  | composite
              | if k >= i  | if k > i   |            |
──────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────┼────────────
SWAP(k,l)     | shift_right| shift_left | composite  | composite
              | if k >= i  | if k > i   |            |
```

### Implementation of Key Transforms

```c
// INSERT vs INSERT: deterministic ordering by priority
crabs_levien_op_t transform_insert_vs_insert(
    crabs_levien_op_t ins_a,  // The one being transformed
    crabs_levien_op_t ins_b   // The concurrent one
) {
    // If ins_a is before ins_b (or same position but lower priority), no change
    if (ins_a.visible_pos < ins_b.visible_pos ||
        (ins_a.visible_pos == ins_b.visible_pos && 
         ins_a.priority < ins_b.priority)) {
        return ins_a;
    }
    // ins_a is after or same position with higher priority — shift right
    ins_a.visible_pos++;
    return ins_a;
}

// DELETE vs INSERT: delete shifts for insertions before it
crabs_levien_op_t transform_delete_vs_insert(
    crabs_levien_op_t del,
    crabs_levien_op_t ins
) {
    if (del.visible_pos < ins.visible_pos) {
        return del;  // Delete is before insert, no change
    }
    // Delete is at or after insert — shift right
    del.visible_pos++;
    return del;
}

// MOVE vs INSERT: move target shifts for insertions
crabs_levien_op_t transform_move_vs_insert(
    crabs_levien_op_t move,
    crabs_levien_op_t ins
) {
    // A move has a source and destination
    if (move.source_pos >= ins.visible_pos) {
        move.source_pos++;
    }
    if (move.dest_pos >= ins.visible_pos) {
        move.dest_pos++;
    }
    return move;
}
```

