## The CRABS Integration Point

The Levien-extended types integrate into CRABS at the **data item level**:

```c
// A CRABS state item can be either:
//   - A basic CRDT type (COUNTER, SET, etc.)
//   - A Levien-extended OT/CRDT type (LEVIEN_ORDERED_SET, etc.)

typedef struct {
    char name[64];

    // Type discriminator
    crabs_data_type_t type;

    union {
        // Basic CRDT value
        crabs_crdt_value_t crdt;

        // Levien-extended value
        crabs_levien_item_t levien;
    };

    // Protocol state (for RESOURCE types)
    crabs_protocol_state_t protocol_state;

    // ... other fields ...

} crabs_data_item_t;
```

### Operation Execution with Levien Types

```c
int crabs_execute_levien_operation(
    crabs_state_t *state,
    crabs_levien_op_t *op
) {
    // Step 1: Get the data item
    crabs_data_item_t *item = crabs_get_item(state, op->item_name);

    // Step 2: Transform against concurrent operations
    for (int i = 0; i < item->levien.op_count; i++) {
        crabs_levien_op_t *existing = &item->levien.op_log[i];

        // Only transform against operations that are concurrent
        // (not causally related)
        if (!causally_before(existing, op) && 
            !causally_before(op, existing)) {
            // Transform op against existing
            *op = crabs_levien_transform(*op, *existing);

            // Also transform existing against op (for future use)
            item->levien.op_log[i] = 
                crabs_levien_transform(*existing, *op);
        }
    }

    // Step 3: Apply the (now transformed) operation
    crabs_levien_apply(item, op);

    // Step 4: Log the operation
    item->levien.op_log[item->levien.op_count++] = *op;

    return CRABS_SUCCESS;
}
```

