## Critical Limitations & Solutions

| Problem | Impact | Solution |
|---------|--------|----------|
| **Doze Mode** | Service throttled, message latency | Use `setAlarmClock` for critical messages; implement message persistence |
| **App Standby** | Daemon killed if unused | Keep persistent notification; use `startForegroundService()` |
| **OEM Killing** | Xiaomi/Samsung/Huawei kill background services | Guide users to whitelist app; use `ACTION_REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS` |
| **Binder Death** | Client crashes don't unregister | Implement `IBinder.DeathRecipient` (shown above) |
| **Transaction Limits** | Binder has ~1MB limit per transaction | Keep messages small; use file URIs for large payloads |
| **Background Starts** | Android 10+ can't start service from background | Clients must bind; use `Context.BIND_ABOVE_CLIENT` |

