## The Companion App Pattern

This is the standard Android equivalent to your desktop service model.

```plaintext
Device Storage:
├── com.yourcompany.pubsub-daemon (Installed once)
│   ├── Native service (C + Binder)
│   ├── Foreground notification (persistent)
│   └── Exported AIDL interface
│
├── com.clientapp.game1 (Depends on daemon)
├── com.clientapp.game2 (Depends on daemon)
└── com.clientapp.utils (Depends on daemon)
```

**How it works:**
1. **Service App**: Standalone app containing your native daemon, published to Play Store
2. **Client SDK**: Lightweight AAR library distributed to app developers
3. **Discovery**: Client apps check for Service App via `PackageManager`
4. **Installation**: If missing, redirect user to Play Store (cannot auto-install)

